Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. GARDEN-CENTRE CAFE - SUNDAY - MORNING

Zoe places three cards: ASK / WATCH / DON'T GUESS. She chooses Meridian's document certification, not her own case.

ZOE
It joins my folder and Voss's jobs without my name. One reference. Watch what changes.

ELIAS
A normal comparison too.

A brief fragment reaches Voss's passive route: MPS-17 / 14:00. No refuge or meeting location. Vale finds the old reference family and prepares a known legitimate control.

INT. PUBLIC LIBRARY - AFTERNOON

Archive laptop packed away. On a public terminal Zoe asks only whether MPS-17-4408 is an authenticated-copy reference. No child identity. At two she submits, logs out and moves when Elias asks.

Automated intake is not an answer.

INT. VOSS AND VALE'S WORKROOM - INTERCUT

Voss calls Meridian's public number for MPS-09-2281, a known legitimate adult file. Routine confirmation. For MPS-17-4408 the clerk stops, requests his name and sends him to compliance. The line disconnects.

Vale writes: SAME QUESTION / DIFFERENT PATH.

Then an old contractor route receives: HISTORIC CERTIFICATION MATERIAL — DO NOT RELEASE.

VOSS
Send nothing back. Now watch.

INT./EXT. LEGAL OFFICE/CAIN'S HOUSE/MAC'S STUDY - AFTERNOON

The restricted-family alert spreads to legal, document-control and sponsor compartments. Mac's solicitor demands who else received it. He cannot stop the automatic distribution.

Cain orders restricted paper copies moved. Mac calls to stop him. Neither accepts the other's responsibility for the missing archive.

CAIN
Then stop people asking questions.

INT. INTERNET CAFE - LATER

Meridian requests Zoe's full identity instead of answering. She does not reply. A temporary handset receives only: CONTROL CLEARED NORMALLY. TEST FLAGGED. CHANNEL WARNING ISSUED.

ZOE
It proves different treatment and wider reaction. Not forgery. Not that every records clerk is criminal.

She records that Voss and Vale asked for no more data.

ELIAS
Evidence towards trust.

ZOE
No more questions yet. Five tells them we're mapping them.

They retire the temporary channel. The archive remains closed all day.

At the motel a car door wakes Zoe. She checks: family, luggage, children. Her heart settles slowly.

ZOE
Fear's faster than evidence.

She returns to the cards. NEXT: FIND WHAT THE FALSE ORDER COPIED.
